# Characterization test: a tracked file's unstaged edit can be overwritten
# by merge. This records current behavior, not a data-safety guarantee.
# Untracked-file protection is checked separately in t30.
I definitions.inc
> init
<<<
+ wug.txt wug.txt
> add wug.txt
<<<
> commit "base"
<<<
> branch dev
<<<
+ a.txt a.txt
> add a.txt
<<<
> commit "master independent change"
<<<
> checkout dev
<<<
+ wug.txt notwug.txt
> add wug.txt
<<<
> commit "dev changes wug"
<<<
> checkout master
<<<
+ wug.txt dev-wug.txt
> merge dev
<<<
= wug.txt notwug.txt
= a.txt a.txt
* .gitlet/Stage/Addition/wug.txt
# Confirm that merge completed and committed the incoming file version.
> log
===
commit [a-f0-9]{40}
Merge: [a-f0-9]{7} [a-f0-9]{7}
${DATE}
Merged dev into master.

===
${COMMIT_HEAD}
master independent change

===
${COMMIT_HEAD}
base

===
${COMMIT_HEAD}
initial commit

<<<*
